  "id": "developmental-psychopathology",
  "term": "developmental psychopathology",
  "definition": "Developmental psychopathology is an understanding of mental and behavioral problems in relation to a person’s development across the lifespan. In this packet, it is presented as part of a biopsychosocial, individualized view that considers how early adversity and other contributing factors shape later symptoms and difficulties.",
